Onboarding Process Overview
1. Payroll Employees
    When an employee is added under Payroll, a New Hire onboarding link is sent to the employee.
    The onboarding status is initially set to New and then moves to Rate Approval.


Onboarding Steps:

1. Employee Completes Onboarding
    The employee fills out and submits all required onboarding information.

2. HR Document Review
    HR reviews the submitted documents:
    Once approved → status becomes Document Approved (Pending I-9 & W-4 via WorkBright)

3. WorkBright Verification
    After I-9 and W-4 are approved in WorkBright → status updates to
    I-9 Submitted (Pending Internal Review)

4. Final Verification
    Once both internal and WorkBright approvals are completed → status becomes Verified
    Completion Logic:
        If HR approves the employee rate request and onboarding status is Verified → status becomes Completed
        If onboarding reaches Verified before rate approval → it will automatically move to Completed after rate approval





2. 1099 Employees
    When an employee is added as 1099:
        The process skips onboarding steps
        Status moves directly from:
            Rate Approval → Completed